  "deletedAt": null,
  "deletedBy": null,
  "details": "Currently if you're using hand tracking or one-handed mode the quick menu spawns at chest-height at a fixed angle. Normally this is fine, however there is a glaring oversight that currently is preventing me from using accessibility features and comfortably playing VRChat.\n\nI currently have my arm in a cast and I want to play VRChat lying down with horizon adjust. I have to lie down ahead of time to calibrate the horizon adjust angle, however since I can only physically use one controller the quick menu spawns at an awkward angle and I cannot interact with it unless I get up. However if I get up I cannot calibrate horizon adjust. See the problem?\n\nOther inconveniences like accessing the whole quick menu also applies when lying down and only using one-handed mode or hand tracking.\n\n(If there were OSC endpoints for horizon adjust and opening the main menu then I could have solved this issue myself...)",
